{"entities":[{"pmid":"8854309","text":"pupillary oscillation","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D011681","start":13,"end":34},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"cocaine","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D003042","start":50,"end":57},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"paranoia","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010259","start":66,"end":74},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"Cocaine","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D003042","start":76,"end":83},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"paranoia","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010259","start":92,"end":100},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"CIP","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010259","start":102,"end":105},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"paranoia","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010259","start":161,"end":169},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"pupillary oscillation","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D011681","start":237,"end":258},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"crack cocaine","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D016578","start":319,"end":332},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"CIP","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010259","start":356,"end":359},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"crack","etype":"Chemical","mesh":"D016578","start":391,"end":396},{"pmid":"8854309","text":"CIP","etype":"Disease","mesh":"D010259","start":421,"end":424}],"gold_relations":"Cocaine | CID | pupillary oscillation\nCocaine | CID | CIP","metrics":{"precision":0.6666666666666666,"recall":1.0,"f1":0.8,"tp":2,"fp":1,"fn":0,"rel_precision":0.6666666666666666,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":0.8,"rel_tp":2,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":0},"pmid":"8854309","relations":["D016578 | CID | D010259","D003042 | CID | D010259","D003042 | CID | D011681"],"text":"A measure of pupillary oscillation as a marker of cocaine-induced paranoia. Cocaine-induced paranoia (CIP) remains an important drug-induced model of idiopathic paranoia for which no psychophysiologic marker has yet emerged. Measures of pupillary oscillation were able to significantly distinguish a group of abstinent crack cocaine abusers endorsing past CIP (n = 32) from another group of crack addicts who denied past CIP (n = 29)."}